      "writtenOn": "2018-07-27T18:48:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "it seems like the framework should be deciding whether or not they need to be flashed.\n\nThis is returning information about the phone.\n\nWouldn\u0027t it be better to know:\n- is the partition bootable\n- is the partition empty\n- etc...\n\nAnd the client can decide if it needs to be flashed?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 106,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "f1db4355f2229689626c75ad0f5bc8ac70b7ca53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b33c78cb_df63d630",
        "filename": "fastboot/1.0/IFastboot.hal",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 107,
      "author": {
        "id": 1120612
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-08-14T19:13:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The information is to identify device-specific partitions who may need some OEM logic to flash them(which cannot be part of fastbootd). The code to flash these partitions would instead be part of the fastboot HAL. Fastbootd can save the list of these partitions and when it receives the command to flash/erase one of them, it can issue the flashPartition method below.",
      "parentUuid": "189b9034_36960b47",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 106,
        "startChar": 53,
        "endLine": 107,
        "endChar": 38
      },
      "revId": "f1db4355f2229689626c75ad0f5bc8ac70b7ca53",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
